# =====================================================================
# Release V047 -- practitioner diary `unavailable` flag (working hours inflated)
# =====================================================================
# Real Dentally rota_practitioner_diaries carries `unavailable` (bool: true = practitioner NOT
# available that day/session). The mock did NOT have it, so Bronze hardcoded Unavailable = 0 with
# the note "field not in API". For real tenants that made EVERY entry look available -- including
# holiday/blocked days that still carry the practitioner's normal 09:00-17:00 hours -- so
# Silver.Available was always 1 and Fact_Practitioner_Diaries.Available_Clinical_Mins counted those
# hours as working capacity. Result: working hours inflated, chair utilisation deflated, and the
# "weird" capacity numbers on the reports.
#
# Fix (SP-only, Bronze): read `unavailable` from stage (Stage.Practitioner_Diary_Entries is
# SELECT * so the column is already exposed -- no view change). CAST covers a bit ('1'/'0') OR a
# string ('true'/'false'); NULL/absent -> available (0). Silver already inverts Unavailable->Available
# and Fact already gates Available_Clinical_Mins on Available=1, so no downstream change is needed.
#
# NB (CREATE-time validation): this references stage column `unavailable`, which exists because the
# real T100 pull landed it. Synthetic tenants (T11/T12) must emit `unavailable` too once the
# generator is reworked (test-data-revisit) or a stage reload without the column would fail the
# CREATE. Fine now -- real stage has it.
#
# AFTER deploy: re-run Orchestrate_Build (build-only, T100). Diary chain updates via the hash gate
# (Unavailable 0->1 changes Silver + Fact hashes), daily aggregate + Fact_Metric_Actuals rebuild,
# so working-hours / chair-utilisation cards correct. No truncate needed.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V047__diary_unavailable_flag.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Bronze.usp_Load_Practitioner_Diary_Entries.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
